<!-- Section 4: NET CLI Commands -->
<div class="card card-shadow p-4 mb-4">
    <h4 class="fw-bold text-primary mb-3">4. Introduction to .NET CLI & Essential CLI Commands</h4>
    <p>The .NET Command-Line Interface (CLI) is a cross-platform toolchain for developing, building, running, and publishing .NET applications.</p>
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-sm table-bordered">
            <thead class="table-light"><tr><th>Command</th><th>Purpose & Example</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet new &lt;template&gt;</code></td><td>Initializes a new project (e.g. <code>dotnet new mvc -n MyMvcApp</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet restore</code></td><td>Restores dependencies and project-specific tools defined in csproj</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet build</code></td><td>Compiles project source code and assets into binary DLL assembly</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet run</code></td><td>Builds and runs the web application immediately</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet watch</code></td><td>Runs application with file-watcher and Hot Reload on code edit</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet test</code></td><td>Executes unit tests using runner (MSTest, xUnit, NUnit)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet publish -c Release</code></td><td>Packages application and dependencies into a folder for deployment</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet add package &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Installs NuGet package into the project (e.g. <code>dotnet add package Dapper</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dotnet ef migrations add</code></td><td>Entity Framework Core CLI for generating code-first database migrations</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 5: C# Code Execution Pipeline -->
<div class="card card-shadow p-4 mb-4">
    <h4 class="fw-bold text-primary mb-3">5. C# Code Execution & Compilation Pipeline</h4>
    <p>C# is a managed language. The compilation and execution flow operates through two main stages:</p>
    
    <div class="p-3 bg-dark text-white rounded mb-3 small" style="font-family: monospace;">
        [ C# Source Code (.cs) ]<br />
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&darr; (Compiled by Roslyn C# Compiler / csc.exe)<br />
        [ Managed Assembly (.dll / .exe) ] &rarr; Contains Common Intermediate Language (CIL/MSIL) + Metadata<br />
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&darr; (Loaded into Common Language Runtime - CoreCLR)<br />
        [ Just-In-Time (JIT) Compiler / RyuJIT ] &rarr; Translates MSIL into Native CPU Instructions<br />
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&darr;<br />
        [ Native Machine Code ] &rarr; Executed directly by CPU with Garbage Collection & Memory Management!
    </div>
</div>

